  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regenerative agriculture advice and software</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This study investigates the gap between the demand by Colombian coffee and avocado smallholder farmers and stakeholders and the potential offer of Dutch knowledge in the field of digital solutions for regenerative agriculture.The smallholder farmers and stakeholders often do not have good access to good quality and affordable agricultural advice. This is due to various factors, including price, remoteness of production location, unfamiliarity of local production conditions by advisers, unavailability of advisers, etc.. In addition, existing software applications for regenerative agriculture are often not applicable to the Colombian context.This study delves deeper into the demand from Colombia in this area and how Dutch companies can adapt their advisory models and tools to the specific agricultural systems in Colombia, such as soil, climate, agricultural traditions, and digital literacy. Based on this study, the Netherlands will be able to better cater to local producers, stimulate the growth of regenerative agriculture in Colombia, resulting in stronger plants, less food loss and chemical inputs, and job creation.</narrative>
  </description>
